From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: Update the device window before applying Reset's fullscreen state.

Painkiller creates a windowed device against the desktop, then resets it
with hDeviceWindow pointing at its initially 640x480 game window. Reset
keeps using m_window from creation until Present updates it. Consequently,
the fullscreen mode, window procedure hook and resize are applied to the
desktop, while presentation switches to the still-small game window.

Select the normalized device window before processing the fullscreen
transition. When an existing fullscreen swapchain changes device window,
leave fullscreen on its old device window first, releasing the old hook,
present rectangle and saved window state. Mark that transition windowed
so the normal path enters fullscreen on the replacement window, including
when both the old and new presentation parameters request fullscreen.

This also resets a temporary Present destination override back to the
device window and invalidates its cached windowed refresh rate. Ordinary
same-window fullscreen resets retain the existing update path.

The issue was reported by DarkSwan86 and Deus-nsf. Blisto91 and BinqAdams
provided the upstream size diagnostics; WinterSnowfall identified the WSI
path and rrPKrr confirmed that resizing the actual game window fixes it.

References:
https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/579
https://github.com/doitsujin/dxvk/issues/3762
---
 src/d3d9/d3d9_swapchain.cpp | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d9/d3d9_swapchain.cpp b/src/d3d9/d3d9_swapchain.cpp
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_swapchain.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_swapchain.cpp
@@ -627,15 +627,32 @@ namespace dxvk {
     this->NormalizePresentParameters(pPresentParams);
 
     bool changeFullscreen = m_presentParams.Windowed != pPresentParams->Windowed;
+    bool changeWindow = m_presentParams.hDeviceWindow != pPresentParams->hDeviceWindow;
+
+    // Reset can replace the device window before the first Present (Painkiller).
+    // Release fullscreen ownership on the old window before switching targets.
+    if (changeWindow && !m_presentParams.Windowed) {
+      m_window = m_presentParams.hDeviceWindow;
+      hr = this->LeaveFullscreenMode();
+      if (FAILED(hr))
+        return hr;
+
+      m_presentParams.Windowed = TRUE;
+    }
+
+    if (m_window != pPresentParams->hDeviceWindow) {
+      m_window = pPresentParams->hDeviceWindow;
+      m_displayRefreshRateDirty = true;
+    }
 
     if (pPresentParams->Windowed) {
-      if (changeFullscreen)
+      if (!m_presentParams.Windowed)
         this->LeaveFullscreenMode();
     }
     else {
       m_parent->NotifyFullscreen(m_window, true);
 
-      if (changeFullscreen) {
+      if (m_presentParams.Windowed) {
         hr = this->EnterFullscreenMode(pPresentParams, pFullscreenDisplayMode);
         if (FAILED(hr))
           return hr;
@@ -643,7 +660,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
       D3D9WindowMessageFilter filter(m_window);
 
-      if (!changeFullscreen) {
+      if (!m_presentParams.Windowed) {
         hr = ChangeDisplayMode(pPresentParams, pFullscreenDisplayMode);
         if (FAILED(hr))
           return hr;
@@ -654,7 +671,7 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
     m_presentParams = *pPresentParams;
 
-    if (changeFullscreen)
+    if (changeFullscreen || changeWindow)
       SetGammaRamp(0, &m_ramp);
 
     UpdatePresentParameters();
